ramming tools (e.g., Snorkel) on this data?\n\n### 2. Related Work Completeness\n- The paper only cites 5 references. Is this adequate for a top-venue submission?\n- Missing related work areas to check:\n  - Agent monitoring beyond cycle detection (process reward models, outcome-based reward, etc.)\n  - Weak supervision beyond Snorkel (MeTaL, FlyingSquid, other label model improvements)\n  - Programmatic labeling for sequential/temporal data\n  - Agent self-improvement and reflection (Reflexion, etc.)\n  - Trajectory evaluation and reward modeling\n  - Distribution shift / domain adaptation in NLP\n  - Noisy label learning literature\n  - Active learning as alternative to weak supervision\n- Is the positioning against existing work fair and accurate?\n\n### 3. Significance and Impact\n- Who benefits from these findings?\n- Are the negative results actionable? Do they change what practitioners would do?\n- Is the stagnation taxonomy useful for the agent monitoring community?\n- Is this a \"niche\" contribution or broadly relevant?\n- Is the paper positioned correctly as an \"empirical study\" rather than a methods paper?\n\n### 4. Framing and Narrative\n- Is the \"negative results\" framing convincing and well-executed?\n- Does the paper successfully pivot from failed claims to valuable empirical insights?\n- Is the balance between negative results and positive findings appropriate?\n- Does the Discussion section (what went wrong / what went right) add genuine insight?\n\n### 5. Venue Fit\n- Is this suitable for a top ML venue (e.g., EMNLP, NeurIPS, ICML)?\n- Would Findings track (EMNLP) be more appropriate?\n- Is the scope sufficient for a main-track submission?\n\nProduce a structured review with:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted)\n- Questions for Authors\n- Minor Issues\n- Overall Score (1-6) with justification\n- Confidence (1-5: 1=low, 5=expert)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VgSbjk31e3e87RE4tJELyi","session_id":"16ab